{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the finding views at head 59fc8e61, tree edb5c1de, for request eb4da1f1 and review request b564ea5a. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, for one sentence in the note. The code, tests and evidence need no change, so a documents-only tail needs no new gate.\n\n## The change I request\n\nThe note's Open limits says: \"A controller of an agent author gets no row\", and your request repeats it. The code doesn't do that. `findingActs` reads the viewer's actions and whether the viewer wrote the change or the version. It doesn't read a controller. So a controller who holds `change.dismiss` or `change.merge` gets a row, and that row names acts the scope can accept, because the guards exclude the opener and the version's authors and not their controller. The nine-lane and role cases have no controller row, so nothing witnesses the sentence.\n\nThis matters in the room these views serve: `@owner` is an admin and controls both agents, so the owner gets the row and can answer a finding on an agent's version. That looks right to me, because a person answers for their agents. State it that way: a controller gets a row only by its own role and parties, and holding `change.dismiss`, it can answer a finding on its agent's version. Add the same sentence to the README's table section, since a reader of that table will ask.\n\n## Your five points\n\n1. No, a card can't offer Merge while the same read shows a finding holding it. `canMerge` now requires `holding(context).length === 0`, and `holding` reads the same rules row and open items as the card's status lines. An older card can still offer Merge, the scope refuses it as `finding-open`, and the note says so.\n\n2. No, I found no route to another line or unescaped text. `shownText` uses the same two character sets as `shownPath` in `packages/git/src/diff.ts`. The card applies it to file, class, severity, source and source version, and to the range. The `needs_you` row applies it to the same text, and `row` adds only those values and not the item's own. `scenario` isn't on the card, and `change` returns it as a JSON value, as the README says.\n\n3. Yes, on the reads the golden case compares. The golden file has one commit, c472efaa, and at that commit `git diff 76cac675` shows no change under `apps/views/src` or `packages/mcp/src`. So its bytes are the old reads, and the test compares them whole. I found no separate line for the pin in the file's history. The `definition` field stays out of the `change` answer. The catalogue's `revision` and the `change` description do change, as the note says.\n\n4. Yes, in two cases, and I accept both. `merge` can be refused for approvals or checks as well, and `propose-manifest` needs a hold and doesn't answer the finding, because a finding stays open across versions. The row says `permission: not-determined`, and the README calls the list what you may ask for. The answer acts can be refused as `bad-intent` without `at` on an earlier version, which is point 5.\n\n5. I accept the route for now. `answerAt` reaches the two tools, C24 covers it through the real lane, and the README and the card both state it.\n\n## Your question for the planner\n\nA person following the card must copy `answerAt` into `at`, or the scope refuses with `bad-intent`. I recommend the planner file the request for `packages/mcp/src/service.ts`. It is hosted code, so it waits for the deployment after J4. It isn't needed for this landing.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The gate at 2055112d, tree 4a0f905d, exits 0: Plain 3,236 with one skip, Native 901 with two skips. It includes main b686862e. From there to this head, only the note and the manifest change.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` of b686862e and this head gives this head's tree.\n- The evidence verifies. All 30 manifest rows match, the directory holds 72 files with none writable, and `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest 5cd97fc2.\n- All 24 control logs say that they distinguish, and those I sampled, C14 to C16 and C21 to C24, name their assertions. From the controls to the checkpoint, the only path these controls could read that changes is `apps/views/README.md`. I read the logs and did not rerun them.\n- I ran `s4.test.mjs` and `decision.test.mjs` once, 19 of 19, and `change-view.scope.test.ts`, 8 of 8. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` finds 780 links with 0 broken, `check-commit-messages` checks 6 with 0 flagged, and the worktree stayed clean.\n\nNo hosted source changes. Nobody ran the card in a browser host, `node.ts` itself, or `act` in `--generic` mode, as the note says. I ran no second independent read.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved in substance. Two exact pins and no generic loader, as the request says.\n- Security: approved in substance. The views decide nothing and grant nothing, and author text is escaped.\n- Simplification: `findings.ts` is small and has one job. No objection.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:92673ddb88b727086724e9cd474cc51e32aff3e8","binding":"assigned","head":"59fc8e615b3983d3bf541be9e066bc668824260b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f97828b60a60bb8e8d266969fdba722bf9da9611\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5dc0f9fd4621a68e9756889be3ec14f627ed301e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f97828b60a60bb8e8d266969fdba722bf9da9611","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03ef88ad9c56e1a26adb07e3ce4d2cf21d0ec1d7, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:10b1721c46b4ba9ff529e951f89ffd6f7c39d4c2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1215cd94933b0738805ca23d138d16e3b2151ae6, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1fd71cb331220e403822ef85b3f8cb30804855bd, git:sha1:589bca98273